## 2. A positive noncentral first-order source

Let `S=R^(1|2)` with parity `(0,1,1)`. Define the real symmetric odd matrix

```text
       [0  1  x]
q(x) = [1  0  0].
       [x  0  0]
```

Its curvature is

```text
       [1+x^2  0   0  ]
F(x) = [0      1   x  ].
       [0      x   x^2]
```

Because `q=q^T`,

```text
F=q^2=q^Tq >=0
```

for every real `x`.

The curvature is not central. With `X=E_12`,

```text
[F(0),X]=X,
{F(0),X}=X.
```

Thus both the Lie/gauge and Jordan/stability shadows remain nonzero at the
selected test point.

