## 4. Normalized closure cost

Use the rank-normalized Hilbert-Schmidt cost

```text
V=(1/2r)Tr(F^TF).
```

The form multiplicity cancels from the normalized trace, so both source and
target give exactly

```text
V(x)=1/3(1+x^2)^2.
```

At `x=0`,

```text
F(0)!=0,
V'(0)=0,
V''(0)=4/3>0.
```

The covariant residual-Hessian split is nontrivial on both sides:

```text
(1/3)||F'(0)||_HS^2       =2/3,
(1/3)<F(0),F''(0)>_HS     =2/3,
full Hessian              =4/3.
```

Therefore this is not a Gram-only example. Half of its stabilizing Hessian is
the residual-contracted second jet identified by H1-T1.

